            <ArticleTitle>Thoracic epidural anaesthesia and analgesia with bupivacaine for transsternal thymectomy for myasthenia gravis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>220-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The present study describes the management of a myasthenic patient undergoing transsternal thymectomy for whom thoracic epidural anaesthesia using 15 mL of bupivacaine 0.5% combined with isoflurane 0.4% and nitrous oxide in oxygen 50% provided good intra-operative relaxation followed by an uneventful recovery and eliminated the need for other post-operative analgesics.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
